{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"SUSE-SU-2025:02391-1","published":"2025-07-19T10:33:34Z","modified":"2026-03-23T04:49:39.541050Z","related":["CVE-2022-49465","CVE-2024-42232","CVE-2024-53146","CVE-2024-53173","CVE-2024-53214","CVE-2024-57893","CVE-2025-21772"],"upstream":["CVE-2022-49465","CVE-2024-42232","CVE-2024-53146","CVE-2024-53173","CVE-2024-53214","CVE-2024-57893","CVE-2025-21772"],"summary":"Security update for the Linux Kernel (Live Patch 58 for SLE 12 SP5)","details":"This update for the Linux Kernel 4.12.14-122_222 fixes several issues.\n\nThe following security issues were fixed:\n\n- CVE-2024-53146: NFSD: Prevent a potential integer overflow (bsc#1234854).\n- CVE-2022-49465: blk-throttle: Set BIO_THROTTLED when bio has been throttled (bsc#1238920).\n- CVE-2024-53214: vfio/pci: Properly hide first-in-list PCIe extended capability (bsc#1235005).\n- CVE-2024-53173: NFSv4.0: Fix a use-after-free problem in the asynchronous open() (bsc#1234892).\n- CVE-2024-57893: ALSA: seq: oss: Fix races at processing SysEx messages (bsc#1235921).\n- CVE-2024-42232: Fixed a race between delayed_work() and ceph_monc_stop(). (bsc#1228959)\n- CVE-2025-21772: partitions: mac: fix handling of bogus partition table (bsc#1238912).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"kgraft-patch-SLE12-SP5_Update_58","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Live Patching 12 SP5","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/kgraft-patch-SLE12-SP5_Update_58&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Live%20Patching%2012%20SP5"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"14-2.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"kgraft-patch-4_12_14-122_222-default":"14-2.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2025:02391-1.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://www.suse.com/support/update/announcement/2025/suse-su-202502391-1/"},{"type":"REPORT","url":"https://bugzilla.suse.com/1229458"},{"type":"REPORT","url":"https://bugzilla.suse.com/1234854"},{"type